# ADDITIONAL MODS #
#F-029_all-trainers # Off by default. Must run before F-010, whose move scripts relocate its Exodar/Silvermoon spawns
#F-010_patch-open-azeroth # Off by default (requires OA map/camera/vmap files, mmaps recommended, core patch + recompile recommended)
#F-013_zep-goblin-start # Off (requires OA, not compatible yet, requires core patch + recompile)
#F-011_mod-druid-forms # Off by default (pseudo-druid forms for ARAC druids; Troll forms are in F-084)
#F-084_troll_druid # Off by default (playable Troll druids with their Cataclysm forms, without the rest of ARAC)
#F-085_tree_of_life # Off by default (Cataclysm lumbering oak Tree of Life per race instead of the treant; keep after the race modpaks and F-011/F-084)
#F-086_travel_form # Off by default (Mists of Pandaria / Battle for Azeroth travel forms instead of the cheetah; keep after the race modpaks and F-011/F-084)
#F-012_mod-extra-models # Off by default
#F-015_mod-instamount # Off by default
F-026_custom-race-support # required for any custom race to function correctly
#F-002_mod-arac # Off by default
#F-087_undead_paladin # Off by default (playable Undead paladins with Forsaken paladin mounts; keep after F-026 and F-002)
#F-003_mod-faction-free # Off by default (core patch in patches/core)
#F-088_mod-two-names # Off by default (hooks for the separate mod-two-names module; core patch in patches/core, client patch in patches/client)
F-089_server-qol # No fatigue and higher .modify limits (core patches in patches/core); comment out for stock behaviour
F-090_mmaps-generator-fixes # mmaps_generator buffer fixes for map ids of 1000 and up (core patch in patches/core)
#F-092_racial-mount-merchant # Off by default (neutral vendor in Booty Bay selling the racial mounts of enabled races; keep after every race modpak)
#F-075_mod-individual-progression # Off by default (for mod-individual-progression: needs its world SQL applied first, patch in patches/individual-progression; keep it last)
#F-076_mod-individual-progression_extras # Off by default (mod-individual-progression's optional SQL and DBCs; one file per feature, delete the ones you don't want, see its readme)
# END ADDITIONAL MODS #